Studio/WebUI constraints:

- Studio/WebUI is an operator/configuration surface, not the authoritative live runtime engine.
- Editable source is `web/showduino-studio/`; generated S3 bundle is `.../WebAssets.generated.h`.
- Prefer editing source modules, then regenerate embed output via existing embed tooling.
- API boundaries: browser calls S3 endpoints/proxy; authoritative show/runtime state comes from P4.
- UI state must not masquerade as authoritative device state.
- Mobile is a first-class target; maintain phone usability and avoid desktop-only assumptions.
- Avoid unnecessary modal chains and avoid making baseline workflows need deep electronics expertise.
- Advanced workflows must not make beginner flows confusing.
- Destructive actions require explicit confirmation.
- Polling/re-rendering must not destroy active form editing state.
- Do not leak credentials/passwords to status JSON, logs, or persistent browser storage unless explicitly designed and justified.
- Do not redesign Studio in unrelated tasks.
